{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104659","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104659/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104659/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104659/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104659","id":2950400801,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc6v24sh","number":104659,"title":"Mouse and touch input fight for control when used simultaneously","user":{"login":"Pixelstyx","id":27587845,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NTg3ODQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27587845?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelstyx","html_url":"https://github.com/Pixelstyx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelstyx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelstyx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelstyx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelstyx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelstyx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelstyx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelstyx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelstyx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelstyx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"ff6055","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":205417413,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDU0MTc0MTM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:windows","name":"platform:windows","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":410064485,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MTAwNjQ0ODU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/needs%20testing","name":"needs testing","color":"ffcc44","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:input","name":"topic:input","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-03-26T17:52:27Z","updated_at":"2025-04-08T20:22:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: every Godot 4 build (regardless of type) from 4.0 stable to the current 4.5.1. Currently happening for me in 4.4.1.stable .NET. and happened to me in 4.3.stable .NET.\n- Also reproducible on other computers with other types of touch devices.\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 - Godot 4.4.1 .NET stable - [Lenovo L13 Yoga](https://www.lenovo.com/ca/en/p/laptops/thinkpad/thinkpadl/thinkpad-l13-yoga/22tpl13l3y1)\n\n### Issue description\n\nUsing any sort of touch device or pen alongside a mouse causes a desync between the system cursor position and Godot's understanding thereof. What this means is that using touch input will often fire events at the system cursor position as well as/rather than where the touch is actually happening. In the in-built text editor, this results in the cursor jumping back to the system position immediately after the tap. My laptop moves the cursor position after the event fires, meaning it's always one touch behind, whereas the pen + tablet I tested with would simply always revert to where the system cursor was.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open a new project.\n- Go to the script tab.\n- Make a bunch of newlines.\n- Move your mouse cursor somewhere down and click.\n- Tap elsewhere in the text editor on a touch screen.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104659/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104659/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}